{
  "_comment": [
    "Example ninfer-supervisor configuration. Copy to supervisor.json and edit.",
    "The real one is gitignored because its paths are machine-specific.",
    "",
    "engine.args is what the supervisor launches. When a models catalog is",
    "present it is rewritten from the selected entry on every switch, so treat",
    "it as derived rather than as the place to edit flags.",
    "",
    "Never put the key in args. Set api_key_file and the supervisor passes",
    "--api-key-file, which keeps the secret off a command line that every",
    "process running as this user can read."
  ],
  "engine": {
    "executable": "P:/NInfer/build-win/apps/Release/ninfer-serve.exe",
    "args": [
      "C:/models/Qwen3.8-27B/qwen3_8_27b_nvfp4_dflash2.ninfer",
      "--host",
      "0.0.0.0",
      "--port",
      "8010",
      "--model-id",
      "qwen3.8-27b",
      "--max-context",
      "32768",
      "--kv-capacity",
      "32768",
      "--max-concurrency",
      "8",
      "--prefill-chunk",
      "2048",
      "--kv-dtype",
      "fp8",
      "--no-prefix-reuse",
      "--spec",
      "dflash2",
      "--draft-tokens",
      "7",
      "--lm-head-draft",
      "--cors"
    ],
    "workdir": "P:/NInfer",
    "api_key_file": "P:/models/ninfer-api-key.txt",
    "engine_host": "127.0.0.1",
    "engine_port": 8010,
    "request_log": "P:/NInfer/supervisor-logs/prod.jsonl",
    "device": 0,
    "unmanaged": false
  },
  "_models_comment": [
    "Edit artifact paths for your machine. Presets share weights but have independent launch settings.",
    "DFlash2 needs the combined companion artifact; see docs/maintainer/qwen3.8-27b-dflash2.md.",
    "Interactive uses DFlash2 K7; concurrent uses MTP K5. Both use a shared 32K KV pool and disable vision and prefix reuse as in the speed qualification.",
    "name and description are optional display text; id selects the preset, --model-id is the client API name.",
    "The model launcher waits for readiness and restores the previous preset on failure."
  ],
  "models": [
